  "reply": "I rewrote `parseDuration` in `src/duration.ts`, and `bun test` passes (26 tests, 0 failures).\n\nThe old regex had a bug (`d+` instead of `\\d+`), so it only matched a literal \"d\" before `ms`. The new version reads the input piece by piece.\n\n- **Accepted:** one or more `h`, `m`, `s` and `ms` components in strictly descending order, with optional whitespace between components and at the ends.\n- **Rejected with `RangeError`:** empty or whitespace-only input, duplicate or out-of-order units, signs, fractions, junk, and any single value or running total above `Number.MAX_SAFE_INTEGER`.\n- **Safe integers:** the total is kept as a `BigInt` and converted to a number at the end.\n- **Whitespace:** I rejected whitespace between a number and its unit (`1 h`), since you only specified it between components. Say so if you want that allowed.\n\nThe export is unchanged, there are no dependencies, and I didn't touch the tests.",
